      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like a pretty lopsided comparison. when you talk about the density side, you're talking about solving a massive housing crisis and fixing climate change, which are huge global problems. but the other side is mostly just talking about \"lifestyle\" and \"tranquility.\" \n\ndoesn't that mean the density argument carries way more weight in a serious policy discussion? if we're looking at it objectively, isn't the single-family preference basically just a matter of personal preference vs. actual societal necessity?",
