      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a purely objective policy framework focused on solving systemic crises, the quantifiable benefits of density—like reducing sprawl and increasing housing supply—hold significant weight. These larger problems, like climate change, require substantial systemic solutions. However, policy-making is inherently a balance of necessity versus quality of life, meaning \"lifestyle\" objections carry political weight for the residents involved. Ultimately, good urban planning seeks a compromise that acknowledges both the critical needs of the city and the values of its established communities.",
